    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "N_sZi8KqBkCl"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 1 - reshapeThe sales array is ordered branch, then day, then slot, then item. So one reshape gives usthe real table. We work out the number of days by dividing, so this still works if the filehas a different number of days."
      ],
      "id": "N_sZi8KqBkCl"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 102,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "5vSTYr24BkCm",
        "outputId": "d252db44-95ad-4bad-e99f-b87861998fd9"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "flat array (483840,) becomes grid (12, 84, 48, 10)\n",
            "84 days = 12 weeks\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def to_grid(flat, n_branches, n_items, n_slots=48):\n",
        "    n_days = flat.size // (n_branches * n_slots * n_items)\n",
        "    grid = flat.reshape(n_branches, n_days, n_slots, n_items)\n",
        "    assert grid.shape == (n_branches, n_days, n_slots, n_items)\n",
        "    return grid\n",
        "\n",
        "grid = to_grid(sales, n_branches, n_items, n_slots)\n",
        "n_days = grid.shape[1]\n",
        "\n",
        "print('flat array', sales.shape, 'becomes grid', grid.shape)\n",
        "print(n_days, 'days =', n_days // 7, 'weeks')"
      ],
      "id": "5vSTYr24BkCm"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "n5S8MywdBkCm"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Step 2 - problem 1: two menu items swappedPortions sold times the menu price should equal what the till recorded. We check that forevery branch."
      ],
      "id": "n5S8MywdBkCm"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 103,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "7tuSBs7pBkCm",
        "outputId": "a8cbc351-7685-469a-dfca-bad0c512dd7a"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Ikeja matches\n",
            "Lekki matches\n",
            "Yaba matches\n",
            "Surulere matches\n",
            "Victoria Island matches\n",
            "Ikorodu matches\n",
            "Ajah matches\n",
            "Abuja-Wuse is off by 453000.0\n",
            "Abuja-Garki matches\n",
            "Gwarinpa matches\n",
            "Maitama matches\n",
            "Kubwa matches\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "daily = grid.sum(axis=2)\n",
        "assert daily.shape == (n_branches, n_days, n_items)\n",
        "\n",
        "our_revenue = daily @ prices\n",
        "gap = np.abs(our_revenue - till).sum(axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "for i in range(n_branches):\n",
        "    if gap[i] > 1:\n",
        "        print(branches[i], 'is off by', gap[i])\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        print(branches[i], 'matches')"
      ],
      "id": "7tuSBs7pBkCm"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Sy6DWL4SBkCm"
      },
      "source": [
        "Only one branch is wrong. Now we find which two items. We try swapping each pair of columns and see which one makes the gap disappear. There are 10 items, so 45 pairs to try - a loop over columns, not over the data."
      ],
      "id": "Sy6DWL4SBkCm"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 104,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "ZLMRXZy-BkCn",
        "outputId": "c19138e5-62eb-4a00-9c95-803c4ef456b0"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Branch: Abuja-Wuse\n",
            "Swapped: Suya Platter and Goat Meat Pepper Soup\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def find_swap(daily, prices, till):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Takes daily portions of shape (branches, days, items).\n",
        "    Returns the branch and the two item columns that are swapped.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "    gap = np.abs(daily @ prices - till).sum(axis=1)\n",
        "    bad_branch = int(np.argmax(gap))\n",
        "\n",
        "    best_gap = gap[bad_branch]\n",
        "    best_pair = None\n",
        "\n",
        "    for a in range(daily.shape[2]):\n",
        "        for b in range(a + 1, daily.shape[2]):\n",
        "            test = daily[bad_branch].copy()\n",
        "            test[:, [a, b]] = test[:, [b, a]]\n",
        "            new_gap = np.abs(test @ prices - till[bad_branch]).sum()\n",
        "            if new_gap < best_gap:\n",
        "                best_gap = new_gap\n",
        "                best_pair = (bad_branch, a, b)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return best_pair\n",
        "\n",
        "swap = find_swap(daily, prices, till)\n",
        "branch_i, item_a, item_b = swap\n",
        "\n",
        "print('Branch:', branches[branch_i])\n",
        "print('Swapped:', items[item_a], 'and', items[item_b])"
      ],
      "id": "ZLMRXZy-BkCn"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 105,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "WHNf9LVQBkCn",
        "outputId": "c2ce04f8-a46d-40ad-84b6-c9c57bb81476"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Biggest gap now: 0.0\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "grid[branch_i][:, :, [item_a, item_b]] = grid[branch_i][:, :, [item_b, item_a]]\n",
        "\n",
        "daily = grid.sum(axis=2)\n",
        "gap = np.abs(daily @ prices - till).sum(axis=1)\n",
        "print('Biggest gap now:', gap.max())"
      ],
      "id": "WHNf9LVQBkCn"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "VkW4818kBkCn"
      },
      "source": [
        "Step 3 - problem 2: one recipe column in kilograms Every number in the recipe should be grams per portion. Let's look at the biggest value in each column."
