    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a4TjVgP-BkCn"
      },
      "source": [
        "Chicken is 300 g a portion, which is sensible. Rice is 0.28, which is not - that is kilograms. We multiply that column by 1000.The loop below checks every column rather than hard-coding rice, so it still works if a different ingredient is wrong in the unseen file."
      ],
      "id": "a4TjVgP-BkCn"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 107,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "_fFaGVOtBkCn",
        "outputId": "76ced19f-d2c6-4a59-ffea-01b9e45b3630"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Rescaled Rice from kg to g\n",
            "Rice is now 280.0 g per portion\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def fix_units(recipe, ingredients):\n",
        "  \"\"\"Takes the recipe sheet of shape (items, ingredients).\n",
        "    Returns it with any kilogram column rescaled to grams. Same shape.\n",
        "    \"\"\"\n",
        "  recipe = recipe.copy()\n",
        "  for k in range(recipe.shape[1]):\n",
        "        biggest = recipe[:, k].max()\n",
        "        if 0 < biggest < 10:\n",
        "            recipe[:, k] = recipe[:, k] * 1000\n",
        "            print('Rescaled', ingredients[k], 'from kg to g')\n",
        "  return recipe\n",
        "\n",
        "recipe = fix_units(recipe, ingredients)\n",
        "print('Rice is now', recipe[:, 0].max(), 'g per portion')"
      ],
      "id": "_fFaGVOtBkCn"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xft0ARoGBkCn"
      },
      "source": [
        "Step 4 - problem 3: closed days. Some days a branch sold nothing at all. That is a closure, not a day when nobody wanted food. If we leave those zeros in, every average gets dragged down. So we replace them with nan and use the nan versions of mean and percentile, which skip them."
      ],
      "id": "xft0ARoGBkCn"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 108,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "YTWV1uAlBkCn",
        "outputId": "2f1258ed-cfbc-4f6d-bbec-4cf4a58d23f2"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Closed branch-days: 31\n",
            "Ikeja closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Lekki closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Yaba closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Surulere closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Victoria Island closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Ikorodu closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Ajah closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Abuja-Wuse closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Abuja-Garki closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Gwarinpa closed on days [25 72]\n",
            "Maitama closed on days [14 15 16 17 18 19 20 25 72]\n",
            "Kubwa closed on days [25 72]\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "closed = daily.sum(axis=2) == 0\n",
        "print('Closed branch-days:', closed.sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "for i in range(n_branches):\n",
        "    days_off = np.where(closed[i])[0]\n",
        "    print(branches[i], 'closed on days', days_off)"
      ],
      "id": "YTWV1uAlBkCn"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 109,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "tl0_rwj4BkCo"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "daily[closed] = np.nan"
      ],
      "id": "tl0_rwj4BkCo"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2rN53c8_BkCo"
      },
      "source": [
        "Here is how much that one change matters:"
