    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "unybTbcrBkCo"
      },
      "source": [
        "Question 1 - how much to order each day. The data starts on a Monday, so if we reshape the days into weeks of 7 the weekdays line up.Then we take the 90th percentile across the weeks: enough to cover demand on 9 days out of 10. Higher than the average, so the branch does not run out, but not so high that food gets thrown away."
      ],
      "id": "unybTbcrBkCo"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 112,
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "bb80ebb5BkCo",
        "outputId": "12e6aa6e-82be-4b40-c530-2d2b4cdba9ec"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "(12, 7, 8)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "weeks = n_days // 7\n",
        "by_week = use_kg[:, :weeks * 7, :].reshape(n_branches, weeks, 7, len(ingredients))\n",
        "assert by_week.shape == (n_branches, weeks, 7, len(ingredients))\n",
        "\n",
        "order = np.nanpercentile(by_week, 90, axis=1)\n",
        "print(order.shape)"
      ],
      "id": "bb80ebb5BkCo"
    },
